# What ships in the VSIX
#
# This file is an allowlist, not a blocklist. Everything in the repository is
# excluded first, then the extension payload is added back one entry at a time.
#
# The reason is the whole point of version 2.0: the extension is native, so the
# package must be provably free of the Python distribution that shares this
# repository. A blocklist can only exclude what someone remembered to name, and
# a new Python module, notebook or fixture added later would silently ship. An
# allowlist cannot fail that way — a new file has to be named here to be
# included. `scripts/audit-vsix.js` re-checks the built archive mechanically.
#
# vsce always includes package.json, and README.md / CHANGELOG.md / LICENSE are
# listed below so the Marketplace page and the license notice are present.

**

!dist/extension.js

!media/icon.png
!media/activity-bar.svg
!media/sql-file-detection-tool-walkthrough.gif
!media/webview/main.js
!media/webview/main.css
!media/walkthrough/open.md
!media/walkthrough/analyze.md
!media/walkthrough/sql.md
!media/walkthrough/azure.md

!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE
